Usage: renice [-n] PRIORITY [-p] PID...  # also: -g PGRP, -u USER [DIFFERS]

Alter the scheduling priority of running processes.
Windows priority classes are mapped to Unix-like niceness values from -20 to 19.

OPTIONS:
  -n, --priority ARG  set niceness value
  -p, --pid           interpret operands as process IDs
  -g, --pgrp          interpret operands as process group IDs
  -u, --user          interpret operands as usernames or UIDs
      --help          display this help and exit
  -V, --version       output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
